  <!-- ========================================================= -->
  <!-- 07. Main UI tooltips -->
  <!-- ========================================================= -->

  <TurkeyLeg_QM_BestPossibleTooltip>Shows the best set your benches could craft if you had the materials. Ignores what's in your stockpiles right now.</TurkeyLeg_QM_BestPossibleTooltip>
  <TurkeyLeg_QM_ArmorCapTooltip>Armor % per body region the optimizer treats as 'enough' (default 200%). Above this, extra armor on that region scores nothing, so utility items are preferred there. RimWorld's effective armor cap is around 200%.</TurkeyLeg_QM_ArmorCapTooltip>
  <TurkeyLeg_QM_ShowCraftedTooltip>Show items you already have - lying on the map or equipped by colonists - so you can compare them against what you can craft. The armor tab keeps its ON THE MAP section; the Weapons and Buffs lists mix the owned items into their rankings (marked owned / equipped / worn).</TurkeyLeg_QM_ShowCraftedTooltip>
  <TurkeyLeg_QM_CreateCustomPresetTooltip>Create a custom preset that chases buffs you pick (e.g. work speed + construction, or research + work speed). It appears as a tab here and uses the same armor/bonuses slider.</TurkeyLeg_QM_CreateCustomPresetTooltip>
  <TurkeyLeg_QM_IncludeSelectedGearTooltip>Also consider the selected pawn's currently worn apparel (no weapons) when picking the best set on the map. Captured when you toggle this or press Refresh list; reselect a pawn and refresh to update.</TurkeyLeg_QM_IncludeSelectedGearTooltip>
  <TurkeyLeg_QM_MaxPiecesTooltip>Cap how many apparel pieces the generated set may use. The optimizer always picks the most valuable pieces first, so a low cap keeps a lean set that gets close to the full result. 20 = no practical limit.</TurkeyLeg_QM_MaxPiecesTooltip>
  <TurkeyLeg_QM_RefreshTooltip>Rescan the map, research, benches, and materials, and rebuild all recommendations.</TurkeyLeg_QM_RefreshTooltip>
  <TurkeyLeg_QM_BlendTooltip>Blend the set between pure protection (left) and this preset's bonus stats (right).</TurkeyLeg_QM_BlendTooltip>
  <TurkeyLeg_QM_ShowUnavailableTooltip>Lists every craftable item in the game, showing the research, bench, or materials you're still missing (in red) for each.</TurkeyLeg_QM_ShowUnavailableTooltip>
  <TurkeyLeg_QM_MinCraftableTooltip>Only count gear your stockpiles could craft at least this many times (any allowed material). Raise it when outfitting the whole colony: an item craftable just once won't gear ten colonists. 1 = show anything craftable at all.</TurkeyLeg_QM_MinCraftableTooltip>
  <TurkeyLeg_QM_ExclusionsTooltip>Hide items, whole mods, weapon classes, or benches from recommendations.</TurkeyLeg_QM_ExclusionsTooltip>
  <TurkeyLeg_QM_OptionsTooltip>Window options: lock/unlock dragging and resizing, reset the position, or open the mod settings (including the classic interface toggle).</TurkeyLeg_QM_OptionsTooltip>
  <TurkeyLeg_QM_ShowTaintedTooltip>Include corpse-tainted apparel in this list (marked tainted). Colonists take a mood penalty for wearing tainted clothing.</TurkeyLeg_QM_ShowTaintedTooltip>
  <TurkeyLeg_QM_HideItemTooltip>Hide this item from recommendations (asks to confirm; Shift-click to skip).
Manage hidden items via the Exclusions button.</TurkeyLeg_QM_HideItemTooltip>
  <TurkeyLeg_QM_PinItemsTooltip>Pin specific items into this category. Pinned items are always included in the generated set (marked "enforced"), and the rest of the set is built around them.</TurkeyLeg_QM_PinItemsTooltip>
  <TurkeyLeg_QM_CreatePolicyTooltip>Create a RimWorld apparel policy allowing only the apparel in the set shown above (including pinned items). Named after the active tab, with a number to avoid clashes. Assign it from a colonist's Apparel tab.</TurkeyLeg_QM_CreatePolicyTooltip>
  <TurkeyLeg_QM_FocusTooltip>Jump to and select this item on the map.</TurkeyLeg_QM_FocusTooltip>
  <TurkeyLeg_QM_RefreshListTooltip>Re-scan items on the map for this set. The list stays put while you equip pieces, so you don't lose your place; press this to re-evaluate against what's left on the map.</TurkeyLeg_QM_RefreshListTooltip>
  <TurkeyLeg_QM_ShowMeleeTooltip>Show or hide the melee section of the weapon list.</TurkeyLeg_QM_ShowMeleeTooltip>
  <TurkeyLeg_QM_ShowRangedTooltip>Show or hide the ranged section of the weapon list.</TurkeyLeg_QM_ShowRangedTooltip>
  <TurkeyLeg_QM_ShowThrowingTooltip>Show or hide the throwing section of the weapon list.</TurkeyLeg_QM_ShowThrowingTooltip>
  <TurkeyLeg_QM_ShowGrenadesTooltip>Show or hide the grenades section of the weapon list.</TurkeyLeg_QM_ShowGrenadesTooltip>
  <TurkeyLeg_QM_ShowLaunchersTooltip>Show or hide the launchers section of the weapon list.</TurkeyLeg_QM_ShowLaunchersTooltip>
  <TurkeyLeg_QM_CollapseBuffTooltip>Click to collapse this buff category.</TurkeyLeg_QM_CollapseBuffTooltip>
  <TurkeyLeg_QM_ExpandBuffTooltip>Click to expand this buff category.</TurkeyLeg_QM_ExpandBuffTooltip>

